    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6304, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5617\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nestablishing the community college funding study\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nRequires a study to consider alternative funding for community\ncolleges.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Adds new subdivision 14 to section 6304 of the education\nlaw to provide that SUNY and CUNY trustees shall require each\ncommunity college president in each of the systems to establish an\ninternal committee directed to study the effectiveness of the current\nfull time equivalent (FTE) funding formula and alternatives.\nCommittees will consider funding of each academic program while taking\ninto account the specific mission, needs, geographic location and\nuniqueness of such community college under review.\n\nThe new subdivision further provides that each internal committee\nshall report recommendations to their university system's board of\ntrustees on December 1, 2017 and the board of trustees of each system\nshall report recommendations to the Chairs of the Senate and Assembly\nHigher Education Committees by January 1, 2018.\n\nSection 2. Sets for the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDuring this year's discussions on community college funding, SUNY put\nforth a \"hold harmless\" model for their community colleges because of\nissues related to enrollment. Because community colleges are funded on\nan FTE model, a school that loses significant enrollment will also\nlose significant operating aid.\n\nThis year alone, SUNY was faced with a cut of over $10 million in\nfunding for community colleges because of decreasing enrollment. This\nlegislation will allow the individual schools and the university\nsystems as a whole, a chance to examine the issue and offer\nrecommendations.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTBD\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
